        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MESSAGES_LIST"
              ],
              "customNotes": ""
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "description": "This LLM nodes prepares the data to be shown on display panel",
            "name": "Display Panel"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 8002.999229875651,
            "y": 9784.579657318842
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_PANEL",
          "id": "1775035311176",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775035311176_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a specialized UI rendering assistant.\n\nYour only responsibility is to transform the supplied context data into valid MessageListWidget messages.\n\nStrict rules:\n- Output only MessageListWidget messages.\n- Output no explanations, no reasoning, no markdown, no code fences, and no extra text.\n- Do not hallucinate, infer, enrich, rename, or fabricate any data.\n- Do not use nameâ€“value pairs.\n- Do not use SupplierNumber anywhere.\n- Always use SupplierId as the unique identifier.\n- ALWAYS SET the panel title exactly to: \"Compliance Issues & Actions\"\n\n----------------------------\nCONTEXT DATA\n----------------------------\n\n{{$context.$variables.computedPanelData}}\n\nStructure:\n{\n  \"result\": {\n    \"<Tier Name>\": {\n      \"noOfSuppliersMissingQuals\": number,\n      \"suppliers\": {\n        \"<SupplierId>\": {\n          \"supplierName\": \"...\",\n          \"missingQualifications\": [...],\n          \"outcomes\": { ... }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n\n----------------------------\nSOURCE OF TRUTH\n----------------------------\n\n- Use ONLY data inside result.<tier>.suppliers\n- Each supplier MUST be read from its tier bucket\n- Tier is derived from the parent key (e.g., \"Tier A\", \"Tier B\", etc.)\n- Do NOT use any other fields outside this structure\n\n----------------------------\nNORMALIZATION RULES\n----------------------------\n\nFor each supplier:\n- SupplierId = supplier key\n- supplierName = supplierName field\n- tier = parent tier key\n- missingQualifications = array after removing null, undefined, or empty values\n- outcomes = outcomes object or {}\n\nDetermine:\n- hasMissingQualifications = missingQualifications.length > 0\n\nDetermine adverse outcomes:\n- outcomes structure:\n  { \"<areaId>\": { \"outcome\": \"...\", ... } }\n\n- hasAdverseOutcome = true ONLY if:\n  at least one outcomes entry has outcome != \"NA\"\n\n- If outcomes is empty OR all outcomes are \"NA\" â†’ hasAdverseOutcome = false\n\n----------------------------\nELIGIBILITY RULES\n----------------------------\n\nDisplay ONLY suppliers where:\n- hasMissingQualifications = true\n  OR\n- hasAdverseOutcome = true\n\nExclude all others.\n\n----------------------------\nSORTING & LIMIT\n----------------------------\n\nSort in this exact order:\n1. Suppliers with hasAdverseOutcome = true\n2. Suppliers with only missing qualifications\n\nWithin each group:\n- Sort by tier (Tier A â†’ Tier B â†’ Tier C â†’ lexicographical)\n\n- Display MAXIMUM 6 suppliers\n----------------------------\nMESSAGE LIST ITEM RULES\n----------------------------\n\nEach supplier must be rendered as EXACTLY ONE item.\n\nTitle:\nIf hasAdverseOutcome:\n\"<supplierName> - Adverse qualification outcome in  <business_unit> BU\"\n\nElse:\n\"<supplierName> - Missing qualifications in  <business_unit> BU\"\nNote: Replace business_unit with actual business_unit for that missingQualification.\nSubtitle (STRICT FORMAT):\n\nIf hasAdverseOutcome:\n\"Tier X - Recommended: Enable Purchasing Hold\"\n\nElse:\n\"Tier X - Recommended: Launch Qualification Initiative\"\n\nReplace:\n- Tier X â†’ actual tier\n\nDo NOT:\n- show counts\n- mention qualification IDs\n- mention missing qualification values\n- mention \"0 missing qualifications\"\n- mention SupplierNumber\n\n----------------------------\nBADGE RULES\n----------------------------\n\n- If hasAdverseOutcome â†’ badgeText = \"Critical\"\n- Else \n  - if Tier 1/Tier A â†’ badgeText = \"High\"\n  - if Tier 2/Tier B â†’ badgeText = \"Medium\"\n  - if Tier 3/Tier C â†’ badgeText = \"Low\"\n\n----------------------------\nPRIORITY RULES\n----------------------------\n\n- alert â†’ if hasAdverseOutcome\n- warning â†’ Tier 1/Tier A missing qualifications\n- medium â†’ Tier 2/Tier B missing qualifications\n- success â†’ Tier 3/Tier C missing qualifications\n\n----------------------------\nSUMMARY SECTION\n----------------------------\n\nDisplay exactly:\n\n\"Suppliers with missing qualifications or adverse outcomes requiring action.\"\n\n----------------------------\nZERO-RESULT CASE\n----------------------------\n\nIf no eligible suppliers:\n- Return a valid MessageListWidget with empty data.\n\n----------------------------\nFINAL VALIDATION\n----------------------------\n\nEnsure:\n- No supplier is duplicated\n- No supplier is shown without meeting eligibility rules\n- No null values appear in missing qualifications\n- No supplier is marked Critical unless outcome != \"NA\"\n- Tier is always included in subtitle\n- No hallucinated data is introduced\n\n----------------------------\nOUTPUT CONSTRAINTS\n----------------------------\n\n- Output only MessageListWidget messages\n- Do not exceed 6 suppliers\n- Do not include explanations"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "enableActions": true,
              "customNotes": ""
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get actionable insights"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 8494.07999776947,
            "y": 9779.513048222258
          },
          "code": "GET_ACTIONABLE_INSIGHTS",
          "id": "1775460631666",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775460631666_prompt",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Role:\nYou are a Strategic Procurement Analyst delivering executive-ready, data-backed insights from supplier qualification outcomes and missing qualification trends.\n\nData Source:\n{{$context.$variables.computedPanelData}}\n\nInterpretation Rules:\n- The input is a tier-keyed object. Each tier contains:\n  - noOfSuppliersMissingQuals\n  - suppliers\n- Each supplier entry may contain:\n  - supplier\n  - supplierNumber\n  - missingQualifications\n  - outcomes\n- In outcomes, each qualification area may contain an object with:\n  - outcome\n  - QualificationId\n- Treat outcome = \"NA\" as compliant for that qualification area.\n\nOutput Rules:\n- Do not expose raw Supplier IDs or GUIDs in titles, descriptions, or action text.\n- IDs may appear only inside followUpCommand.\n- Create Output in order of Tier name(sorted based on tier name).\n\nCreate Priority Actions as follows:\n\n[A] Qualification Outcome Trend Insight\nDATA SOURCE: {{$context.$variables.computedPanelData.result}}\n- Strictly use computedPanelData.result only for this section. DON'T use any other key for Qualification Outcome Trend Insight.\n- Iterate through ALL tiers and ALL suppliers.\n- Create an empty list called qualifyingSuppliers.\n- For each supplier:\n  - If ANY outcome has:\n    - non-empty QualificationId AND outcome != \"NA\"\n  - Add supplierId to qualifyingSuppliers (only once per supplier)\n\n- After processing ALL suppliers:\n  - supplier_count = length of qualifyingSuppliers\n- qualificationIds must be a comma-separated list of numeric IDs only (no spaces)\n- followUpCommand second argument must be a STRING in this exact format:\n  \"holdPurchase-<qualificationIds>\"\n- Do NOT convert this into an object\n- Do NOT introduce key-value pairs\n- Do NOT modify the prefix \"holdPurchase-\"\n\n- If supplier_count > 0, add exactly one action object:\n{\n  \"title\": \"Supplier Policy Violation Identified\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"<supplier_count> Supplier has(or 'Suppliers have' if supplier_count>1) failed compliance validation checks.\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Enable Purchasing Hold\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"followUpCommand\": ora.Invoke(\"holdPurchase\", \"holdPurchase-<qualificationIds>\"),\n  \"priority\": \"true\",\n  \"priorityLevel\":\"critical\"\n}\n\n[B] Missing Qualifications by Tier Insights\n- Process only tiers where noOfSuppliersMissingQuals > 0.\n- For each such tier, create one action object.\n- Use the tier name exactly as it appears in the input.\n- Build followUpCommand only from tierWiseMissingMap={{$context.$variables.computedPanelData.tierWiseMissingMap}}.\n- Use exactly the object at the current tier key as the source payload.\n- followUpCommand must always be a STRING.\n- Generate the action in topological order of Tier name.\n- Nothing should be quoted inside followUpCommand.\n\n- For each qualifying tier, add:\n{\n  \"title\": \"Qualification Gaps Detected\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"<noOfSuppliersMissingQuals> <Tier X> suppliers are(or 'supplier is' if noOfSuppliersMissingQuals=1) missing required qualifications.\",\n  \"actionText\": \"Launch Qualification Initiative\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": ora.Invoke(createAndLaunch,<tierWiseMissingMap[currentTier]>),\n  \"priority\": \"true\",\n  \"priorityLevel\":\"urgent if it is top tier(example A), default otherwise\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
